.Rproj.user/
.Rhistory
.RData
*.rds
*_cache/
*_files/
index_cache/

# ...BUT the rendered book is SITE CONTENT, not an R build artefact (2026-09-04).
# `*_files/` matches at ANY depth, so it also swallowed `integrated_bioanalytics/book/index_files/` —
# the 553 figure PNGs the published book links to 199 times — and `*.rds` swallowed
# `integrated_bioanalytics/data/protein_embeddings_example.rds`, which chapter 14 fetches.
# This lay dormant for as long as those files were already TRACKED (gitignore never untracks). It only
# detonated when the tracked set was rebuilt from scratch (`git rm -r --cached .` + re-stage): the
# re-stage skipped every ignored path, and the resulting commit DELETED the book's figures.
# Negations must follow the rule they undo, and a file cannot be re-included while its parent directory
# is excluded — hence the directory line as well as the `/**` line.
!integrated_bioanalytics/book/index_files/
!integrated_bioanalytics/book/index_files/**
!integrated_bioanalytics/data/*.rds
# Deliberately still ignored: `_bookdown_files/` (render cache), `z_archive/**` (already ignored above),
# and the top-level `Integrated Bioanalytical Chemistry.rds` (a bookdown intermediate — verified
# unreferenced by any chapter or rendered page).

# OS files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# script
members_update.py

# Deploy driver (maintenance script, not site content). Same posture as members_update.py: it lives in
# the tree and reaches the Mac via Syncthing, but does not belong in a PUBLIC repo — untracked it would
# otherwise be served at https://thebustalab.github.io/deploy.sh. No secrets in it; this is tidiness plus
# not advertising the publish workflow. NOTE: gitignore does not untrack an already-committed file — if it
# ever got committed, run `git rm --cached deploy.sh` once on the Mac, then commit.
deploy.sh

# Lab Quests (labelling) backend source — carries the real ACCESS_KEY + sheet IDs
# when configured. It's a source reference only, NOT served (the live backend runs
# in the Apps Script cloud), so keeping it out of this public repo is safe. The
# served page (labelling/index.html) stays tracked. NOTE: gitignore does not
# untrack an already-committed file — run `git rm --cached labelling/apps_script.gs.js`
# once on the Mac, then commit.
labelling/apps_script.gs.js

# Blog research (private, not for public repo)
blog/literature/
blog/online-research/

# Escape-rooms authoring: rolling scenario.json backups the harness writes on every save
escape_rooms/**/scenario.json.bak
# Escape-rooms authoring: the whole _scratch candidate pool is local authoring churn (~20 MB/scenario
# of gpt-image-2 candidates) — never needed at play time (the player reads the committed room dirs +
# scenario.json). Keeps the pushed site lean. (Supersedes the old _scratch/draft.json line.)
escape_rooms/**/_scratch/
